    <preface xml:id="preface">

        <p>This text is intended to be a home to test the interactive components of <pretext/>.  It is based on the book <em>Abstract Algebra: Theory and Applications</em> by Thomas W. Judson, which is available at <url href="http://abstract.ups.edu" visual="abstract.ups.edu"/>.  The original text was written for a one-semester course in abstract algebra, and it is assumed that the reader has had a course in linear algebra and some experience with proofs.</p>

        <p>We will organize it by chapters and each chapter will highlight things that are fully accessibile and not so accessible.  The goal is to have a fully accessible text, but we are not there yet.  We will also highlight the interactive components of <pretext/> that are available in this text.</p>

    </preface>

